WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.559
The CrestApps Report Builder lets the people who run your site build their

00:00:05.559 --> 00:00:09.263
own reports by dragging fields, instead of writing queries.

00:00:09.263 --> 00:00:13.196
This video shows why it exists, how to build, chart and share a

00:00:13.196 --> 00:00:15.760
report, and every data source it reads.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.586
Your site keeps its data in many places:

00:00:23.586 --> 00:00:32.000
content items, users and roles, contact center calls, omnichannel activities, AI chat sessions, and text messages.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:36.812
Built-in reports answer the questions someone thought of in advance.

00:00:36.812 --> 00:00:40.600
A new question used to mean asking a developer for a new query.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:45.872
The Report Builder puts the answer in the hands of the people asking.

00:00:45.872 --> 00:00:51.480
They pick data sets, join them, group and total them, add charts, and share the result.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:01.038
A data source is the data of one module, such as Contents or Contact Center.

00:01:01.038 --> 00:01:07.180
Each source offers data sets, such as Activities or Users, and each data set has fields.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:14.312
A report combines data sets, picks columns and filters, and shows the result in visuals:

00:01:14.312 --> 00:01:17.910
tables, charts, metric strips and pivot tables.

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:21.473
A view is a saved, reusable data set.

00:01:21.473 --> 00:01:27.490
Other reports use its columns like any other fields, and it can refresh on a schedule.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.522
Everything respects permissions.

00:01:30.522 --> 00:01:34.607
A data source shows only what the person may read, and a saved

00:01:34.607 --> 00:01:37.430
report runs with the access of its owner.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:46.075
Turn on the Report Builder feature under Tools, Features.

00:01:46.075 --> 00:01:49.981
The Reports (OpenXml) feature adds Excel exports.

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:54.172
The Report Builder appears under Reports in the admin menu.

00:01:54.172 --> 00:01:58.024
It lists every report you can open, and the filter at the top

00:01:58.024 --> 00:02:00.324
shows published reports or drafts.

00:02:00.778 --> 00:02:04.589
From the list, run a report, edit it, or delete it.

00:02:04.589 --> 00:02:10.738
The Actions menu clones a report into your own copy, which is not shared with anybody.

00:02:14.919 --> 00:02:16.558
Click New report.

00:02:16.558 --> 00:02:18.839
The builder has four tabs:

00:02:18.839 --> 00:02:22.189
Settings, Design, Data model and Sharing.

00:02:22.643 --> 00:02:26.987
On the Settings tab, give the report a title, a description and a

00:02:26.987 --> 00:02:32.983
category, and choose whether it appears in the admin menu and whether viewers may export it.

00:02:33.435 --> 00:02:36.218
On the Design tab, add a data set.

00:02:36.218 --> 00:02:41.855
The list groups the data sets by source; pick Activities, from Omnichannel.

00:02:42.305 --> 00:02:44.855
Its fields appear in the Data pane.

00:02:44.855 --> 00:02:49.645
Drag a field onto Columns, and the preview shows the result right away.

00:02:50.096 --> 00:02:52.604
Add Number of rows to count them.

00:02:52.604 --> 00:02:56.978
With a count, the report groups the rows by its other columns:

00:02:56.978 --> 00:02:59.936
here, activities per channel and status.

00:03:00.389 --> 00:03:04.548
A new report starts filtered on the last thirty days of its main

00:03:04.548 --> 00:03:07.934
date, which keeps reports over a lot of data quick.

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:10.489
You can change or remove that filter.

00:03:14.692 --> 00:03:18.117
Click a column to edit it under Properties.

00:03:18.117 --> 00:03:22.869
An aggregate turns a number into a sum, an average, a count, a

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:26.712
distinct count, a minimum, a maximum or a median.

00:03:27.168 --> 00:03:30.473
A transform changes a value before grouping.

00:03:30.473 --> 00:03:34.703
For a date, pick the day, the week, the month or the year,

00:03:34.703 --> 00:03:36.818
to see activity over time.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:42.791
Give each column a header and a format, such as one decimal place or a percentage.

00:03:42.791 --> 00:03:47.370
Hide a column from tables while keeping it for grouping and charts.

00:03:47.823 --> 00:03:53.890
Calculated fields use formulas, with functions for text, numbers, dates and aggregates.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:56.370
This one is the completion rate:

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:59.893
the completed activities divided by all of them.

00:04:00.345 --> 00:04:05.625
Drag the calculated field onto Columns, and it works like any other field.

00:04:09.812 --> 00:04:11.869
Drag a field onto Filters.

00:04:11.869 --> 00:04:15.211
A row filter narrows the data before grouping.

00:04:15.211 --> 00:04:20.802
A result filter applies after it, such as channels with more than ten activities.

00:04:21.258 --> 00:04:25.337
Let viewers change this filter, and pick how they choose:

00:04:25.337 --> 00:04:30.257
a drop-down list, a list with several choices, a recent period, a date

00:04:30.257 --> 00:04:32.588
or number range, or yes or no.

00:04:33.041 --> 00:04:38.168
Exposed filters appear above the report, as searchable lists filled with the values

00:04:38.168 --> 00:04:39.551
found in the data.

00:04:39.551 --> 00:04:41.971
Viewers pick values and click Apply.

00:04:46.142 --> 00:04:50.259
Visuals are listed under Visuals, in the order they appear.

00:04:50.259 --> 00:04:53.362
A table shows the rows, and can add totals.

00:04:53.817 --> 00:04:56.648
Add a chart, and pick its type:

00:04:56.648 --> 00:05:00.857
bar, horizontal bar, line, area, pie or doughnut.

00:05:00.857 --> 00:05:04.837
Then pick the category and the values to plot.

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:11.073
A metric strip shows a few key numbers at the top of the report.

00:05:11.523 --> 00:05:15.857
A pivot table puts one column down the side and spreads the values

00:05:15.857 --> 00:05:17.783
of another across the top.

00:05:18.801 --> 00:05:22.973
Set the width of each visual to place them side by side.

00:05:22.973 --> 00:05:29.501
Charts, metrics and totals regroup the underlying rows, so an average stays a true average.

00:05:33.686 --> 00:05:35.338
Add a second data set:

00:05:35.338 --> 00:05:36.046
Users.

00:05:36.046 --> 00:05:40.471
Data sets that reference each other, such as an activity and the user

00:05:40.471 --> 00:05:43.066
it is assigned to, are joined for you.

00:05:43.519 --> 00:05:47.718
The Data model tab draws the data sets and their relationships.

00:05:47.718 --> 00:05:53.013
To join two yourself, drag a column of one onto the matching column of the other:

00:05:53.013 --> 00:05:57.029
here, the campaign of an activity onto the ID of a campaign.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:00.604
Click a relationship to set its type:

00:06:00.604 --> 00:06:05.400
inner, left, right or full, on one or more pairs of columns.

00:06:05.853 --> 00:06:10.701
Back on the Design tab, the fields of both data sets are available.

00:06:10.701 --> 00:06:14.353
Here, activities are counted per user and status.

00:06:18.536 --> 00:06:20.632
A report can be only data.

00:06:20.632 --> 00:06:27.706
This campaign summary is a plain table, with viewer filters, a calculated completion rate, and totals.

00:06:28.159 --> 00:06:30.865
A report can combine charts and data.

00:06:30.865 --> 00:06:34.830
This one shows a metric strip, a bar chart and a table of

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:36.969
activity outcomes per agent.

00:06:37.421 --> 00:06:39.705
Tables can show subtotals.

00:06:39.705 --> 00:06:45.130
With Role, Agent and Status, there is a subtotal for each agent within

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:48.771
a role, one for each role, and a grand total.

00:06:49.221 --> 00:06:54.091
Pie charts and pivot tables suit shares and cross-tabs, such as the share

00:06:54.091 --> 00:06:57.481
of each disposition, and dispositions by channel.

00:07:01.683 --> 00:07:06.928
Contents offers one data set per content type, with its parts and fields.

00:07:06.928 --> 00:07:13.633
Owners, content pickers and user pickers reference other data sets, so they join automatically.

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:18.085
Users offers the accounts of the site and their roles.

00:07:18.085 --> 00:07:22.080
Passwords, tokens and other secrets are never exposed.

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:29.042
Contact Center offers interactions, call sessions and their quality, queues and queue items,

00:07:29.042 --> 00:07:33.760
agent profiles and sessions, callbacks, voicemail and recordings.

00:07:34.211 --> 00:07:39.688
Omnichannel offers activities, dispositions, campaigns and activity batches.

00:07:39.688 --> 00:07:46.501
AI Chat offers chat sessions and their metrics, and Messaging offers conversations and messages.

00:07:46.952 --> 00:07:50.927
Saved queries, and the views you build, are data sets too.

00:07:50.927 --> 00:07:53.412
Modules can add their own sources.

00:07:57.598 --> 00:08:00.718
Every change is saved in a draft as you work.

00:08:00.718 --> 00:08:05.978
Close the page and come back later, and the builder picks up where you left off.

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:11.143
Click Publish to make the changes live for everybody who can open the report.

00:08:11.143 --> 00:08:13.130
Each publish keeps a version.

00:08:13.582 --> 00:08:16.354
Versions lists every published version.

00:08:16.354 --> 00:08:18.388
Preview one, or restore it.

00:08:18.388 --> 00:08:22.947
When two people edit the same report, the builder shows who else has

00:08:22.947 --> 00:08:26.952
it open, and stops one from silently overwriting the other.

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:34.614
Report Views lists the reusable data sets.

00:08:34.614 --> 00:08:37.002
Build a view like a report:

00:08:37.002 --> 00:08:41.560
data sets, joins, calculated fields, filters and columns.

00:08:48.211 --> 00:08:50.603
Choose how often it refreshes:

00:08:50.603 --> 00:08:55.320
every fifteen minutes, every hour, every six hours, or every day.

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:59.971
A background task stores the result, so reports read it quickly.

00:09:00.426 --> 00:09:05.259
In any report, the view appears under the Report views source, and its

00:09:05.259 --> 00:09:07.866
columns are fields like any others.

00:09:12.037 --> 00:09:16.337
On the Sharing tab, share the report with users, and with roles.

00:09:18.877 --> 00:09:22.722
Share links let people without an account open the report.

00:09:22.722 --> 00:09:26.267
Each link can expire, and can be revoked at any time.

00:09:26.721 --> 00:09:32.341
A shared report reads data with your access, so share only what viewers should see.

00:09:32.794 --> 00:09:37.694
Viewers run the report, change its filters, and export it as a C

00:09:37.694 --> 00:09:40.494
S V file, or as an Excel workbook.

00:09:44.694 --> 00:09:49.121
Developers add a data source by implementing IReportDataSource.

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:54.126
It lists its data sets, describes their fields, and returns rows for the

00:09:54.126 --> 00:09:56.114
fields a report asks for.

00:09:56.864 --> 00:10:04.474
For data kept in records, derive from ReportRecordDataSource, and register the source with the service collection.

00:10:04.474 --> 00:10:07.644
The source decides what each person may see.

00:10:08.394 --> 00:10:13.814
The data source skill in the repository walks through every contract, step by step.

00:10:15.814 --> 00:10:20.463
The Report Builder turns the data of your site into reports that anyone

00:10:20.463 --> 00:10:22.455
can build, chart and share.

00:10:22.455 --> 00:10:24.024
Thanks for watching.

